    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/nfdi4cat/goldbook-skos/blame/main/vocabularies/goldbook/IDs00xxx/00245.ttl> ;
    skos:definition "The group $\\ce{CH2=CHCH2}$ (allyl) and derivatives formed by substitution. The term 'allylic position' or 'allylic site' refers to the saturated carbon atom. A group, such as $\\ce{–OH}$, attached at an allylic site is sometimes described as 'allylic'."@en ;
